[Music]  [Applause]  chris angel reveals his seven-year-old  son johnny's cancer is in remission more  than six years after his diagnosis  today is johnny christopher day and we  want to thank all of you for the amazing  love and prayers and support  over the years  johnny was diagnosed with acute  lymphoblastic leukemia in october 2015  when he was just 20 months old  my reaction in that moment was  disbelief  i thought it happened to  the other person  not to you  he initially went into remission in june  2016 and eti was with chris shortly  before the cancer returned in 2019. we  get blood tests every  month or two and everything is coming  back with all signs saying that he's  remaining in remission and we pray that  he remains there for the rest of his  life fast forward to 2022 and good news  johnny is back in remission  chris who shares johnny with chenille  benson celebrated his son's improved  health by sharing a 13-minute short film  titled 10.95 which represents the total  number of days he was in treatment  we've spent most of johnny's life in and  out of clinics and hospitals and  it's so weird it feels like it's just  normal now you know what i mean like  we're here  so much that it's it's kind of part of  our home  the 54 year old magician released a  short film on instagram monday and in a  press release chris explains quote this  is our family story but it's really the  story of every family unfortunate enough  to have a child with cancer this  horrible disease impacts not just the  children but all those that love them  our hope is that as many people as  possible can see 1095 and be moved to  help so we can continue to raise  awareness improve treatment and one day  find a cure  one child every two minutes is diagnosed  with cancer  cancer doesn't discriminate i want to  try to be a voice for these kids i want  to try to help  these families that are going through  the toughest time of their life  and  let them know that they're not alone  you know what i mean  there's magic in the world and that  magic is love  chris adds on instagram that the short  film which shows footage from the  doctor's visits and emotional private  moments is quote the most important post  he's ever shared if i could take this  disease from him i would in a heartbeat  and before asking his followers to watch  and share the project to raise awareness  and help find a cure chris writes quote  today our son johnny christopher will  finally ring the bell symbolizing his  remission and the end of his treatment  i feel like all of this success that  i've been so blessed to have is really  for a greater cause and that is  pediatric cancer one child every two  minutes is diagnosed with it so if you'd  like to help out you can go to  chrisangel.com click the help button and  donate and know that 100 of every cent  you donate will go to research and  treatment for these children suffering  with this horrible disease  [Music]  you

